message: "If you use this software or the reference solutions it contains, please cite both the archived software and the accompanying paper."
title: "Near-body zoning and interface overlap in extended physics-informed neural networks for sparse-data flow reconstruction"
abstract: >-
  Code and CFD reference solutions for a controlled ablation of subdomain zoning
  and interface overlap in extended physics-informed neural networks (XPINNs),
  applied to the reconstruction of steady flow fields from sparse measurements.
  Includes the four decomposition configurations for each of four benchmarks
  (circular cylinder at Re = 40, NACA 0012 at Re = 1,000 and Re = 10,000, and the
  Turek-Hron FSI1 configuration), the reference solutions generated with FEniCS,
  SU2 and turtleFSI, post-processing and baseline scripts, and the aggregated
  results underlying every value reported in the accompanying paper.
